acct_note_display_name = Display name is optional -- leave it blank to send as this account's own name.
acct_note_identity = The email address can differ from the login email if your provider has a custom domain linked to this mailbox. Mail will be sent and received under the address above, while sign-in still uses the login email. Leave the password field blank to keep the password already stored for this account -- for example after rotating a Gmail app password, type the new one here; otherwise leave it blank.
acct_note_identities = Other addresses this account can send and reply as. Replying to a message that was sent to one of these defaults From to that address instead of the one above.
acct_note_signature = Appended to every new message, reply and forward sent from this account, below a "-- " line. Leave blank for none. Edit Signature opens the formatted editor, where bold, lists and links are available; the box above then holds the plain text version that goes out alongside it.
acct_note_junk = Which real folder Mark as Junk moves messages to. "{automatic}" uses the same provider-aware guess Archive and Trash already use; set this only if that guess is wrong or your junk folder has a custom name.
acct_note_disable = A disabled account is never contacted -- no IDLE, no periodic refresh, nothing -- until re-enabled. It still shows in the tree, marked (disabled), and its already-downloaded mail stays available offline. Same toggle as Accounts > Disable Account or the account's own context menu; this is just another place to reach it.
acct_note_default = This account's folders appear first in the tree, and a new message defaults to sending from it unless changed manually in the composer. Does not affect which address a reply or forward uses -- that already follows the message being answered (see Additional Identities above). There is always exactly one default account, so unchecking this on the current default without checking it on another one leaves it unchanged -- check another account's box instead to hand the default to it.
acct_note_mute = Muting blocks this account's new-mail sound, spoken announcement and Windows notification, regardless of how those are otherwise configured. It does not affect other accounts, and it's still subject to the master switches in Settings > Sound & Notifications (sounds and desktop notifications overall).
wiz_note_app_password = If you already have an app password created for ZBox, press Next to continue.
wiz_note_login = Login credentials.\nIf your login email is different from the address above, for example your provider account is login@example.net but you want to send and receive as you@example.org, enter the login email here. You can set the custom send address afterward in Account Settings.
wiz_note_servers = Server settings, pre-filled where the domain is recognized. Edit anything that needs to be different.
wiz_preset_none = No preset found for this domain. Enter your provider's server settings manually; your provider's help pages will list them.
ab_note_groups = Type a group's name in a compose window's To, Cc or Bcc field to fill in every one of its members at once.
cache_note_intro = These remove ZBox's local copies only. Nothing is deleted from any mail server, and a removed message is downloaded again the next time you open it.
cache_note_age = Automatic clean up runs once a day, when ZBox has had no keyboard activity for ten minutes and no message is open. It goes by each message's own date, including messages that are still in your account.
filt_note_intro = Rules run in order, top to bottom, testing From, To and Subject. Applied automatically to new mail as it arrives in this account's Inbox; use Run Now below to apply them to messages already sitting in a folder.
filt_note_run_now = Applies every enabled rule above, in order, to every message already in the chosen folder -- saves your changes first, the same as OK.
mp_note_intro = These accounts were set up on another computer. Enter the master password to unlock their saved passwords here. You will only be asked once on this computer.\n\nWithout it, each account has to be signed in to its mail server again.
priv_note_remote = Images, stylesheets and fonts that a message loads from the internet tell the sender the moment you opened it, and from where. With this on, none of them load: a notice appears above the message saying what was blocked, and Ctrl+Shift+I loads it for that one message. Pictures attached to the message itself always show. Scripts and embedded frames are removed either way and are never loaded.
priv_note_blocklist = This is the second layer. It matters once you load a message's remote content, or allow a sender: the pictures load, but anything served from a known tracking or advertising domain still does not. The list is downloaded from public ad and tracker lists and merged; updating takes a second or two and runs in the background.
priv_note_junk = No guessing. Mark as Junk adds the sender to the blocked list below, unless the message came through a mailing list. Mark as Not Junk adds the sender to the never-junk list and that message is never checked again. A new message from a blocked sender is marked Blocked Sender in the list; one that links to a known phishing or malware site is marked Possible Phishing. Your mail provider's own spam filtering still runs as before.
priv_status_phishing_updating = Phishing list: updating in the background. Reopen this dialog to see the result.
priv_status_updating = Updating in the background. Reopen this dialog to see the result.
rel_note_intro = Messages related to "{subject}" by their Message-ID/References headers, across every folder in this account.
srch_note_intro = Search From, Subject and Body for text you enter below. Searches every account and folder unless you narrow it below.
sig_note_plain = Leave the plain text alternative blank and it is written from the formatted signature when you press OK.
unified_note_intro = Choose which folders to combine across every account. Each one checked becomes a single entry in the tree that combines that folder from all your accounts.

